                <pb facs="0131" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv10/pg121"/>

                <head>Appendix 59</head>
                <p rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum From the Shipping Section
                        Regarding</hi>] <hi rendition="#italic">Yugo-Slam Ships in the
                    Adriatic</hi></p>
                <p>Paragraph 5 of the Naval Clauses of the Armistice with Austria Hungary provided
                    that Austro-Hungarian ships found at sea should be made subject to capture
                    unless exceptions are made by a Commission <pb facs="0132" n="122"
                        xml:id="pg122"/> to be appointed by the Allies and the U. S. A. It appears
                    that this qualification was intended to apply specially to ships owned by
                    Yugoslavs and that such ships, nominated by the Commission, would be released
                    from the provisions of the Armistice applying to enemy ships.</p>
                <p>An appeal has been received from the Serbian representative in Paris<anchor
                        n="12" xml:id="d10-f1"/> pointing out that no action has been taken by the
                    Commission of the four Admirals in the Adriatic to except any Yugo-Slav ships,
                    and requesting that a Commission should be appointed to act in the spirit of
                    Clause 5 of the Armistice conditions.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-26">26 <hi rendition="#small-caps">March</hi>,
                        1919</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
